# PC5's own attributes. The LFS block below is inherited from the repository's earliest days
# and is load-bearing: `.pup`/`PS5UPDATE.PUP` routing is what keeps the protected firmware
# input a *pointer* rather than bytes in the tree (docs/research/PS5_FIRMWARE_AND_PUP.md; the
# incident recorded in ci/README.md). The rules that used to sit above it were a Unity
# project's -- `merge=unityyamlmerge` on `.mat`/`.unity`/`.asset`/`.meta` -- for file types
# this repository has never contained, and with no such driver configured they were inert at
# best and misleading at worst (debt D-2). They are replaced by rules for the tree PC5 has,
# in the same number of lines so that a citation of a line number here cannot silently drift.
*.cs diff=csharp text eol=lf
*.xaml text eol=lf
*.csproj text eol=lf
*.props text eol=lf
*.sln text eol=lf
